Biopsies are essential diagnostic procedures for monitoring the progression of Cystic Fibrosis. By analyzing tissue samples, healthcare professionals can identify abnormalities and assess the effectiveness of treatment strategies. This underscores the importance of regular monitoring and the role of biopsies in the comprehensive management of FQ, ensuring that patients receive timely and appropriate care. [Data: Entities (490); Relationships (3583)]

