The mutation of the ATP7B gene is directly associated with the development of Enfermedad de Wilson, making genetic testing an important aspect of diagnosis. Additionally, clinical indicators such as Kayser-Fleischer rings and levels of ceruloplasmin are critical for diagnosing and monitoring the disease. Understanding these genetic and diagnostic factors is essential for timely intervention and management of Wilson's disease. [Data: Entities (11783, 11869); Relationships (9231, 9246)]# Patient Care Community: Nutritional and Medical Management

