Antioxidants such as vitamin C and vitamin E are important in reducing oxidative stress associated with Alzheimer's disease. Vitamin C acts as an antioxidant that may help mitigate cellular damage in the brain, while vitamin E has been shown to protect against cellular damage, which is particularly relevant for Alzheimer's patients. These vitamins highlight the importance of incorporating antioxidant-rich foods into the diets of individuals with Alzheimer's disease. [Data: Entities (13262, 13263), Relationships (1912, 1914)]# Vitamin E and Related Health Conditions

