FGF23 is a phosphaturic protein that is ectopically expressed in mesenchymal tumors associated with osteomalacia oncog√©nica. It plays a crucial role in regulating phosphate metabolism, influencing urinary phosphate excretion, and affecting vitamin D synthesis. The secretion of FGF23 by tumors leads to decreased levels of calcitriol, which in turn impacts calcium and phosphate absorption, contributing to the symptoms of osteomalacia oncog√©nica. Understanding FGF23's role is essential for developing targeted therapies for affected patients. [Data: Entities (5722); Relationships (8405, 15134)]

