Mesenchymal tumors are polymorphic neoplasms that can cause osteomalacia oncog√©nica by secreting FGF23 and other phosphaturic proteins. These tumors can be located in various anatomical sites, including long bones, distal extremities, and soft tissues. Their slow growth and varied presentation can complicate diagnosis, making awareness of their potential to cause osteomalacia oncog√©nica critical for healthcare providers. [Data: Entities (5723); Relationships (15133, 15136, 15135)]

