## Health benefits of legumbres

Legumbres are recognized for their substantial health benefits, particularly in reducing cholesterol levels and lowering the risk of cardiovascular diseases. They are a vital source of protein and fiber, making them essential in healthy diets, including the Mediterranean diet. The consumption of legumbres is associated with a decrease in the incidence of colorectal cancer, further emphasizing their role in promoting health. This is supported by multiple data references [Data: Entities (655); Relationships (4495, 4497)].

