## Importance of lipid emulsions in parenteral nutrition

Lipid emulsions such as SMOFLIPID, LIPOFUNDINA, and LIPOPLUS are essential components of parenteral nutrition, providing necessary fats and calories for patients who cannot eat orally. These emulsions are specifically formulated to meet the unique nutritional requirements of pediatric patients, especially newborns, who are at risk of malnutrition due to their medical conditions. The use of these emulsions is crucial in ensuring that patients receive adequate nutrition for growth and recovery, particularly in clinical settings where traditional feeding methods are not viable. [Data: Entities (2550, 2549, 2735); Relationships (4691, 4690, 4928)]

