The lipid emulsions in this community, including SMOFLIPID, LIPOFUNDINA, and LIPOPLUS, feature diverse formulations that cater to specific patient needs. For instance, SMOFLIPID combines soybean oil, medium-chain triglycerides, olive oil, and fish oil, while LIPOFUNDINA focuses on a balanced mix of medium-chain and long-chain triglycerides. LIPOPLUS incorporates omega-3 fatty acids, which are known for their anti-inflammatory properties. These variations in formulation are crucial for addressing the unique metabolic requirements of different patient populations, particularly in pediatric care. [Data: Entities (2550, 2549, 2735); Relationships (10168, 10162, 10159)]

