Zidovudina is an antiretroviral medication used in the treatment of HIV/AIDS. Its relationship with Metformina indicates its role in the comprehensive management of patients who have both diabetes and HIV. This dual management approach is crucial for improving the overall health outcomes of patients with coexisting conditions, showcasing the need for integrated treatment strategies in chronic disease management. [Data: Entities (14305); Relationships (13583)]

