Allergies are classified as diseases that can severely impact health, influenced by genetic and environmental factors. They represent a major public health issue, particularly as they can lead to various adverse reactions, including food allergies that manifest early in life. The relationship between allergies and the immune system is crucial, as the immune response to allergens can lead to serious health complications. This highlights the importance of understanding allergies within the broader context of health and disease management. [Data: Entities (9026), Relationships (4312)]

## The role of genetic polymorphisms

