Glutamine has been studied as a potential treatment to alleviate the symptoms of mucositis in patients undergoing hematopoietic cell transplantation. Research indicates that oral administration of glutamine can reduce both the duration and severity of mucositis, making it a beneficial intervention for affected patients. This finding emphasizes the importance of exploring various treatment options to improve patient comfort and nutritional status during cancer treatment [Data: Relationships (7772)].

