NPT is frequently initiated for patients post-surgery who are unable to meet their nutritional needs through oral intake. This practice is vital for ensuring that patients receive the necessary nutrients to support healing and recovery after surgical procedures. The connection between NPT and post-surgical care highlights the therapy's importance in critical care settings. [Data: Relationships (8913)]

