The research conducted by BROWN and BROCKLEHURST has significant clinical implications, particularly in the context of hematopoietic transplantation. Understanding fragility and its determinants can lead to better patient management strategies, potentially improving recovery outcomes. The identification of fragility through physical function tests, as suggested by BROWN, could allow healthcare providers to tailor interventions more effectively. This research underscores the need for ongoing studies in this area to refine clinical practices and enhance patient care. [Data: Relationships (10868)]# Morbimortalidad and Critical Health Factors

