Length of hospitalization is often prolonged in critically ill patients due to complications arising from conditions like malnutrition and multi-organ dysfunction. This extended duration can lead to increased healthcare costs and resource utilization, emphasizing the need for effective management strategies to reduce hospitalization times and improve patient outcomes. Understanding the factors that contribute to prolonged stays is essential for optimizing care in critical settings [Data: Entities (12873); Relationships (1356, 1355, 1341, 1342, 1354, +more)].# EHC and Royal Free Hospital Community

