## EHC patients' vulnerability to malnutrition

Patients with EHC are particularly vulnerable to malnutrition, which can lead to severe health complications. This vulnerability is a significant concern in the nutritional management of these patients, as malnutrition can exacerbate their condition and lead to increased morbidity and mortality. The relationship between EHC and malnutrition highlights the urgent need for effective nutritional interventions to improve patient outcomes. [Data: Relationships (7285, 1339)]

