Systemic inflammation is a response that can be triggered by cancer, contributing to malnutrition and weight loss in patients. Elevated levels of inflammatory markers, such as C-reactive protein, are often observed in patients with esophageal cancer, indicating a link between inflammation and the disease's progression. This relationship underscores the importance of monitoring inflammatory responses in cancer patients to tailor nutritional and therapeutic strategies effectively. [Data: Entities (13373); Relationships (585, 16400)]

## Odynophagia as a debilitating symptom

Odynophagia, or pain during swallowing, is a common and distressing symptom for patients with esophageal cancer. This condition significantly impacts their ability to consume food and liquids, leading to further nutritional deficiencies and weight loss. Addressing odynophagia is critical in the management of esophageal cancer, as it directly affects patients' quality of life and nutritional status. Effective pain management and dietary modifications are essential components of care for these patients. [Data: Entities (13372); Relationships (583, 16399)]

