## Acute renal failure as a critical condition

INSUFICIENCIA RENAL AGUDA, or acute renal failure, is a serious medical condition that requires immediate intervention. It is characterized by a sudden loss of kidney function, which can lead to severe complications if not managed properly. The condition often necessitates intensive care and specific nutritional management to support recovery. The interconnectedness of various treatments and nutritional strategies is crucial for patient outcomes. [Data: Entities (2183); Relationships (9121, 9123, 9127)]

## Role of hemodialysis in treatment

HEMODI√ÅLISIS is a vital treatment for patients with acute renal failure, as it helps filter waste products from the blood when the kidneys are unable to perform this function. This procedure is essential in clinical settings, particularly in intensive care units, where patients may experience severe complications. Hemodialysis not only addresses immediate health needs but also significantly impacts the nutritional requirements of patients, necessitating careful dietary adjustments. [Data: Entities (2191); Relationships (9120, 9145)]

## Importance of peritoneal dialysis

DI√ÅLISIS PERITONEAL serves as an alternative treatment for patients with renal failure, utilizing the abdominal lining to filter waste from the blood. This method is particularly beneficial for individuals with chronic kidney disease and requires careful management of caloric intake due to the glucose present in the dialysis fluid. The relationship between peritoneal dialysis and nutritional management is critical for ensuring patient health and recovery. [Data: Entities (2200); Relationships (9127, 2640)]

