A heart-healthy diet, which is low in saturated fats and aims to reduce LDL cholesterol levels, is crucial for hospitalized patients. This dietary approach must include appropriate macronutrients to support overall patient health, particularly for those with cardiovascular concerns. The relationship between macronutrients and heart-healthy diets underscores the importance of balanced nutrition in managing health outcomes [Data: Entities (1788); Relationships (7606)].

