NEUMON√çA ASPIRATIVA is a serious complication that can arise from the use of enteral feeding tubes, including nasoenteral tubes. This condition occurs when food or liquid inadvertently enters the lungs, leading to respiratory issues. The risk of aspiration pneumonia underscores the importance of proper tube placement and monitoring during enteral feeding. It is crucial for healthcare providers to be aware of this risk and implement strategies to minimize it, ensuring patient safety during nutritional support. [Data: Entities (14573); Relationships (7920, 16096)]

