Nutritional Intervention is essential in the treatment of Anorexia Nervosa, focusing on restoring healthy eating patterns and preventing refeeding syndrome. This intervention is tailored to meet the unique dietary needs of individuals suffering from this condition, emphasizing the importance of a structured approach to nutrition in recovery. By addressing these needs, nutritional intervention plays a significant role in improving the health and recovery of patients with Anorexia Nervosa. [Data: Relationships (11383)]

