Gastrinomas, glucagonomas, and somatostatinomas are frequently associated with the genetic condition MEN1, indicating a significant clinical relationship. MEN1 is a syndrome that predisposes individuals to multiple endocrine tumors, and a substantial percentage of gastrinomas are found in patients with this condition. This connection underscores the importance of genetic screening and monitoring for individuals diagnosed with MEN1, as they are at a higher risk for developing these tumors. [Data: Relationships (12601, 12603, 12604)]

