Hypercortisolism is characterized by excessive cortisol production, often evaluated in patients with adrenal incidentalomas. The diagnosis involves measuring cortisol levels, which is critical for understanding the patient's hormonal status and potential health implications. This condition can be associated with various health issues, including eating disorders, highlighting the need for careful assessment and management [Data: Entities (4956); Relationships (12234, 11993)].

## Tissue resistance to glucocorticoids

Tissue resistance to glucocorticoids occurs when the body's tissues do not respond effectively to glucocorticoid hormones, leading to symptoms of excess hormones. This condition can complicate the management of diseases where glucocorticoids are typically used as treatment, necessitating alternative therapeutic approaches [Data: Entities (5096); Relationships (12229, 14645)].

