## Dexamethasone's role in treating Cushing syndrome

Dexamethasone is a key therapeutic agent for Cushing syndrome, a hormonal disorder characterized by excessive cortisol levels. It works by suppressing adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) levels, which is crucial for managing the symptoms and underlying causes of this condition. The relationship between Dexamethasone and Cushing syndrome underscores the importance of this medication in clinical settings, particularly for patients suffering from this disorder. [Data: Entities (5095, 5191); Relationships (12544)]

