The McCune-Albright syndrome is a genetic disorder that is often associated with precocious puberty, particularly in females. This relationship highlights the need for comprehensive evaluation in patients presenting with early sexual development, as underlying genetic conditions may complicate treatment and management strategies. [Data: Entities (5287); Relationships (12040)]

