## Cardiovascular diseases as a leading health threat

Cardiovascular diseases are a major health concern, particularly in Western countries, where they are the leading cause of death and disability. These diseases are influenced by various modifiable risk factors, including dietary habits, lifestyle choices, and nutritional intake. The prevalence of these diseases underscores the importance of understanding their causes and implementing preventative measures. [Data: Entities (3172); Relationships (11179, 11176, 11177, 13168, 14848, +more)]

