Several foods, including C√∫rcuma, Ar√°ndanos, and Espinaca, contain oxalate, which can increase the risk of kidney stone formation. Individuals prone to nephrolitiasis are often advised to limit their intake of high-oxalate foods to manage their condition effectively. Understanding the oxalate content in various foods is crucial for dietary planning. [Data: Entities (1516, 4647, 11981); Relationships (6596, 13901, 14284, 14282)]

## Citrus juices as protective agents

Citrus juices, particularly those high in citrate, are recognized for their potential protective effects against kidney stones. The citrate content in these juices can help increase urinary citrate levels, which is beneficial in reducing the risk of stone formation. Incorporating citrus juices into the diet may be a valuable strategy for individuals at risk of nephrolitiasis. [Data: Entities (11980); Relationships (14277)]

