Refeeding syndrome is a potentially fatal condition that can occur when feeding is resumed in malnourished individuals, especially those recovering from anorexia nervosa. This syndrome highlights the risks involved in reintroducing nutrition to patients who have experienced starvation or severe malnutrition. The condition necessitates careful management and monitoring during the refeeding process to prevent serious complications. The relationship between refeeding syndrome and anorexia nervosa underscores the importance of understanding this syndrome in the context of nutritional rehabilitation. [Data: Entities (8955); Relationships (17234)]

