## Oxidative stress as a contributing factor

Oxidative stress is linked to the development of Alzheimer's disease and other neurodegenerative conditions. It refers to an imbalance between free radicals and antioxidants, leading to cellular damage. Understanding the role of oxidative stress in Alzheimer's disease is crucial for developing effective interventions, as it may provide insights into dietary and lifestyle changes that could help manage or prevent the disease. [Data: Entities (3204); Relationships (11310, 11308)]

