Nutritional factors play a vital role in the management of frailty syndrome. Specifically, caloric-protein supplementation has been shown to combat weight loss and improve health outcomes in frail elderly individuals. This highlights the importance of addressing nutritional needs as part of a comprehensive treatment plan for frailty, ensuring that elderly patients receive adequate support to maintain their health and independence. [Data: Entities (3126, 3136), Relationships (11086, 11095)]

