The relationships among IDL, LDL, Apo E, and PCSK9 illustrate a complex network of interactions that are essential for cholesterol metabolism. Each entity plays a specific role in the metabolic pathways, and disruptions in these relationships can lead to dyslipidemia and associated health risks. This interconnectedness emphasizes the importance of a holistic approach to studying lipid metabolism and its implications for cardiovascular health. [Data: Relationships (15497, 15516, 15517, 15518)]# Lipoprotein Metabolism Community

