Parenteral nutrition is often necessary for patients with hepatopathy, especially when enteral nutrition is contraindicated. However, the risk of developing liver disease increases with long-term parenteral nutrition, highlighting the need for careful management of nutritional support. This relationship underscores the complexity of treating patients with liver conditions and the importance of monitoring liver health in those receiving parenteral nutrition. [Data: Relationships (4633, 8769)]

