The Harris-Benedict equation is a key tool used to estimate the energy requirements of patients receiving nutritional support. This equation is particularly important for calculating caloric needs in patients experiencing hypermetabolic states, such as those with polytraumatism or traumatic brain injuries. Its application ensures that patients receive adequate nutrition tailored to their specific metabolic demands. [Data: Entities (2111); Relationships (8935, 8934)]# Nutritional Support Community: Vitamins and Parenteral Nutrition

