Hypomagnesemia is a critical medical condition defined by insufficient magnesium levels in the body, which can lead to severe health complications. It is often associated with various factors, including malnutrition, alcoholism, and certain medications. The condition is particularly concerning in hospitalized patients, where it has been linked to increased mortality rates. Addressing hypomagnesemia through appropriate supplementation and dietary management is essential for improving patient outcomes. [Data: Entities (2337); Relationships (3401, 762, 5794, 7287, 9598, 941, 9596, 8696)]

