## Legumbres as a staple in healthy diets

Legumbres are recognized for their health benefits, particularly in reducing cholesterol levels and lowering the risk of cardiovascular diseases. They are a vital source of protein and fiber, making them a staple in healthy diets, including the Mediterranean diet. Dietary guidelines recommend consuming legumbres 1-2 times a week, preferably in homemade preparations rather than canned versions. This emphasis on legumbres highlights their importance in promoting overall health and well-being [Data: Entities (655); Relationships (4505, 4495, 4504)].

