Legumbres are recommended as a source of protein in children's diets, according to pediatric nutritional guidelines. This highlights the importance of incorporating legumbres into the diets of younger populations to ensure adequate nutrition. However, caution is advised regarding the consumption of miel by infants due to the risk of botulism, emphasizing the need for careful dietary management in vulnerable groups [Data: Entities (7931); Relationships (4500, 16858)].

