## Total Energy Expenditure is crucial for dietary planning

Total energy expenditure (GASTO ENERG√âTICO TOTAL) is a vital metric for determining the energy needs of individuals, especially in clinical settings. It encompasses various components, including basal metabolic rate, thermic effect of food, and energy used during physical activity. For instance, in patients with specific health conditions like cancer, their total energy expenditure may be lower than expected, necessitating tailored dietary plans to meet their unique needs. This is particularly important for ensuring adequate nutrition and energy balance in these populations [Data: Entities (1786); Relationships (7633, 7635, 7630)].

