## Denys-Drash syndrome's genetic basis

Denys-Drash syndrome is primarily caused by mutations in the WT1 gene, which plays a crucial role in kidney development and sexual differentiation. The presence of these mutations leads to severe health issues, including progressive kidney disease and the risk of Wilms tumor, a type of kidney cancer. The severity of the syndrome underscores the importance of genetic testing and monitoring for affected individuals. [Data: Entities (5400, 5403); Relationships (14900)]

